From: =?UTF-8?q?Kenan=20Kasumovi=C4=87?=
 <46025606+Ken5998@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:58:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] main: write stdout and stderr to the files named by
 PORT_STDOUT/PORT_STDERR

Proton's launcher starts the game without std handles, so everything the
runtime prints (telemetry, warnings, errors) was lost on the ARM64 port.
The port's launch script names the log files instead.
---
 infamous-recomp/main.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/infamous-recomp/main.cpp b/infamous-recomp/main.cpp
index 3e54600..c16c2b9 100644
--- a/infamous-recomp/main.cpp
+++ b/infamous-recomp/main.cpp
@@ -893,6 +893,11 @@ int main(int argc, char** argv)
 #ifdef _WIN32
     /* v241C LOG_ASYNC drain helper process (see v241c_la): nothing else runs in it */
     if (argc >= 2 && strcmp(argv[1], "--v241c-logdrain") == 0) return v241c_la::helper_main(argc, argv);
+    /* PORT_STDOUT / PORT_STDERR (default unset = nothing): files for stdout / stderr. The Windows launchers start the
+     * game with both redirected to play.out.log / play.err.log; Proton's launcher starts it with no std handles, so
+     * the ARM64 port names the files here. Before the first stdio access (configure_stdout_buffering). */
+    { const char* o = getenv("PORT_STDOUT"); if (o && *o && !freopen(o, "w", stdout)) return 70;
+      const char* e = getenv("PORT_STDERR"); if (e && *e && !freopen(e, "w", stderr)) return 71; }
     /* v242B PS3_AFFINITY=<hex mask> (default unset = nothing): restrict the whole process to those logical CPUs
      * BEFORE any thread exists (weak-PC emulation / user choice). bench_drive's BENCH_AFFINITY only applies the mask
      * after the start, so threads sized at boot saw all CPUs. Bits outside the system mask are ignored. */
